  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment and Business Member Organizations (EBMOs) continue to lose members, struggle to collect subscriptions regularly and to respond to issues related to the informal economy and the changes in the world of work and business occasioned by the megatrends in technology, climate change, globalisation and demographic changes. EBMOs are offering services limited to industrial and labour relations. No other services are provided, to SMEs and other players in the informal economy. 
A service needs assessment to identify the gaps in the provision of Financial and Business Development Services was undertaken with a view to starting to offer services to SMEs and informal economy. EBMOs face challenges in advocating for an enabled business environment and to inform interventions and measures to influence an enabling environment for sustainable enterprises in Zimbabwe. They require support to adapt service provision to existing and new members- revamp their communication and advocacy platforms to allow for members and non-members to access information that is vital for their operations. 
During the 2024-2025 the ILO will support EBMOs towards - increased institutional capacities to be strong, independent and representative- in analysing the changing business environment and conduct advocacy activities to influence policymaking towards enabling environments for entrepreneurship, sustainable enterprises, decent work and productivity growth.</narrative>
  </description>
